eeding tubes is critical for the success of nutritional interventions in patients unable to consume food orally. [Data: Entities (14604); Relationships (16167, +more)]", "# Yeyunostomía Quirúrgica and Related Procedures\n\nThe community focuses on the surgical procedure of yeyunostomía quirúrgica and its associated components, including the use of catéter fino, potential complications, and the técnica de Witzel. These entities are interconnected through their roles in providing nutritional support to patients unable to eat normally.\n\n## Yeyunostomía quirúrgica as a central procedure\n\nYeyunostomía quirúrgica is a significant surgical procedure that provides nutritional support to patients who cannot eat normally. This procedure is crucial in the context of gastrointestinal surgery, as it helps to avoid risks associated with parenteral nutrition. The importance of this procedure is underscored by its relationships with other entities, indicating its central role in the community. [Data: Entities (14596); Relationships (16163, 19932, 19933, 19931)]\n\n## Role of catéter fino in yeyunostomía\n\nThe catéter fino is an essential component used in the yeyunostomía quirúrgica procedure, facilitating direct feeding into the jejunum. Its role is critical as it ensures that patients receive the necessary nutrition post-surgery. The relationship between the catéter fino and the yeyunostomía quirúrgica highlights the technical capabilities required for successful surgical outcomes. [Data: Entities (14603); Relationships (19932)]\n\n## Potential complications of feeding tubes\n\nComplicaciones de las sondas de yeyunostomía refer to the potential issues that can arise from the use of feeding tubes, such as obstruction and infection. Understanding these complications is vital for healthcare providers to mitigate risks associated with the procedure. The relationship between these complications and the yeyunostomía quirúrgica emphasizes the need for careful monitoring and managem